    "problem": "Effect of Oxygen Defects Blocking Barriers on Gadolinium Doped Ceria (GDC) Electro-Chemo-Mechanical Properties Some oxygen defective metal oxides, such as cerium and bismuth oxides, have recently shown exceptional electrostrictive properties that are even superior to the best performing lead-based electrostrictors, e.g. lead-magnesium-niobates (PMN). Compared to piezoelectric ceramics,\u2026",
